          "reasoning": "On sysmonlinux-ctus-attack-range-6628, user ubuntu used an interactive bash session (proc-e55f41e475) to write a script with nano (soloshred.sh), check it with cat, and then run shred -n 1 -x -z three times in quick succession: twice against /usr/lib/systemd/system and once against /boot (the trigger, proc-3d1967b5ac). Pointing shred's overwrite and zero-fill options at boot and systemd directories is data destruction (T1485) that can leave the host unbootable. Nothing in the graph suggests a sanctioned admin purpose. Response: isolate the host, rotate the ubuntu account's credentials, delete the script and its swap file, and check that /boot and the systemd unit directory are intact.",
